mode: "100644"
text: "# The STYLE framework — style as choices, tone as control\n\nStyle isn't decoration; it's a sequence of choices a reader feels. This framework runs as edit passes on any\ndraft (human or AI-assisted). Most \"sounds like ChatGPT\" pain is a missing S (nothing only-you) and a missing\nL (no rhythm); most brand-damage pain is a missing T (wrong tone, right voice).\n\n## S — Sound like someone\nThe anti-slop core: the disease isn't em dashes — it's sentences anyone could have written. Every piece\ncarries at least one thing **only this writer could say**: a real number from their work, a named moment, a\nstated opinion, a lived detail. Concrete beats abstract (\"31 of the last 40 receipts arrived after 10pm\"\nbeats \"clients often send receipts late\"). Subjectivity is a feature — human writing takes positions and\nwanders productively where AI stays neutral and rigidly on-topic. The voice itself (vocabulary, stance, humor)\ncomes from `voice-builder`; this gate makes each piece *inhabit* it.\n\n## T — Tune tone to the moment\n**Voice is identity (constant); tone is register (flexes).** Build the tone map once: celebration = full\npersonality · education = warm, clear, unhurried · sales = confident, restrained · complaint response = human,\naccountable, un-clever · crisis/bad news = plain, direct, zero playfulness. The voice's fingerprints\n(vocabulary, rhythm) persist underneath every register — a playful brand announcing layoffs goes plain, not\ncorporate-anonymous. Platform register shifts the same way: length/formality adapt, identity doesn't (the\ncover-the-handle test: regulars should recognize the writer anywhere).\n\n## Y — Yank the dead weight\nThe subtraction pass: **fluff sentences** (professional-sounding, information-free) deleted whole ·\nthroat-clearing openers cut (\"In this post I'll…\") · hedges trimmed to the ones that carry real uncertainty ·\nadjectives doing a verb's job replaced (\"moved fast\" → \"shipped in nine days\") · one idea per sentence ·\nfront-load the point. If a line can vanish without loss, it already had.\n\n## L — Let the rhythm breathe\n**Burstiness — sentence-length variation — is the human signature** the monotone draft lacks. Alternate\ndeliberately: a long sentence that builds and builds, then a short one. That lands. Punctuation is pacing, not\nornament; paragraphs on social run short; plain words beat impressive ones. **The universal test: read it\naloud** — where you stumble or run out of breath, the reader already left. (First-line hook craft routes to\n`hook-writer`; this gate owns everything after it.)\n\n## E — Edit against the tells, intelligently\nThe final pass runs the tell **cluster** — hallmark vocabulary, \"It's not X, it's Y,\" forced rule-of-three,\nrigid structure, misplaced social proof, relentless positivity — with judgment, not bans: no single marker\nproves anything, detector-score theater optimizes for the wrong judge, and the Stanford finding (a 61.3%\naverage false-flag rate on non-native-English essays) shows what cargo-cult hunting costs. The real question is the substance test from S: *does\nthis say something only we could say?* If yes, punctuation panic is noise. Disclose AI use where platform or\npolicy requires; then the human signs off and **WoopSocial publishes.**\n"
